        "description": {
            "value": "<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> Will (negates; willing targets automatically allow the mark)</p><p>You leave an invisible sign on a creature, door, or object. Once, at a moment of your choosing while within 1 mile, you sense that the marked thing has crossed a threshold, changed hands, or come to harm (the GM sets the specific trigger when you cast this). Old churches carved marks in doorframes for the same reason: so someone, someday, would know you'd been there.</p>"
